00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:30,480
Following, following our launch, it was like, So tell us what happened there.

166
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:32,240
So you launched as a free app, right?

167
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:35,280
With a with a single lifetime in app purchase.

168
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,120
That was the original model.

169
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:38,800
We had a whole strategy.

170
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:40,800
It was we were so proud of the strategy.

171
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:42,960
We're still in the chat.

172
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:46,480
It's like, so we had it was a free app.

173
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:48,720
Well, let me let me tell you, let me tell you just the.

174
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:52,000
high level strategy and then I'll tell you how we applied that strategy in our launch.

175
00:13:52,160 --> 00:14:02,800
Our strategy had always been, we want to get millions of people using Darkroom for free to create our own user base that we can build more premium features over time and upsell them on it.

176
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:07,760
And we had two content types that we wanted to sell people on.

177
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,360
One was filters, filter packs.

178
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:13,760
This was in the days of it was basically VSCO and Snapseed and nothing else, 2015.

179
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:18,400
And so we wanted to recreate the VSCO business model of selling filter packs.

180
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:21,840
And the other was selling premium tools, the Snapseed model.

181
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:24,880
And so we wanted to do that.

182
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:26,880
And so that was that was what we went in.

183
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:29,280
And that's actually, in large part, our strategy today.

184
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:42,080
Create as many people using Darkroom for free, provide like a ton of value so that they get bought in to our way of thinking about mobile photography and then continue adding value add into our premium tier so that people will switch.

185
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:46,480
The problem was we were selling filter packs.

186
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:52,080
We were selling four filter packs at launch and two tools and we were selling everything independently.

187
00:14:52,640 --> 00:15:00,800
